  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Highlights' / 'Summarized key operating and financial data' summary table (audited). Converted from a conventional bank (NRB Global Bank) to a Shariah-based Islamic bank (Global Islami Bank) during 2021; pre-2021 terminology ('loans and advances', 'classified loans') and post-2021 terminology ('investment', 'classified investment') both map to the same normalised fields here. Bank converted to a full-fledged Shariah-based Islamic bank and rebranded from NRB Global Bank to Global Islami Bank during 2021. Regulatory capital surplus/(deficit) against the minimum capital requirement was NEGATIVE (BDT -1,528.21mn) — i.e. GIB's Total Regulatory Capital fell short of the Bangladesh Bank minimum requirement in FY2021, a capital-adequacy breach. Precise CAR% for this year was not located in the source documents (only the underlying capital-fund and surplus/deficit figures), so is left as a gap rather than estimated.",
